1. Introduction

The **AI-Powered Student Support and Smart Campus Intelligence System** aims to use Artificial Intelligence and Deep Learning to improve student support and campus services.

Our team is responsible for the **Data Preparation & Evaluation Testing** module. This module ensures that the data used by AI models is clean, reliable, properly structured, and representative. It also provides systematic methods to evaluate and test model performance.


2. Problem Statement

AI models depend heavily on the quality of their training data. Campus datasets may contain:

- Missing values
- Duplicate records
- Inconsistent formats
- Incorrect labels
- Noisy data
- Imbalanced classes
- Data leakage
- Train/test contamination

Poor-quality data can result in inaccurate and unreliable AI predictions.


3. Proposed Solution

We propose a structured pipeline to prepare, validate, and evaluate data before it is used by AI models.

```text
Raw Data
   ↓
Validation
   ↓
Cleaning
   ↓
Preprocessing
   ↓
Annotation & Labeling
   ↓
Quality Verification
   ↓
Dataset Versioning
   ↓
Train / Validation / Test
   ↓
Benchmark
   ↓
Model Evaluation
   ↓
Regression Testing

This pipeline will act as the quality layer of the Smart Campus AI system.

4. Aim

To develop a reliable and reproducible framework for preparing high-quality datasets and systematically evaluating AI models used in the Smart Campus system.

5. Objectives

Collect relevant campus and student-support datasets.
Validate and clean raw data.
Handle missing values, duplicates, and inconsistencies.
Preprocess and normalize data for Deep Learning.
Annotate and label datasets accurately.
Maintain dataset versions.
Create reliable train, validation, and test sets.
Develop benchmark datasets and test cases.
Evaluate model performance using suitable metrics.
Perform regression testing after model or dataset updates.

