7. Data Quality Checks

Before a dataset is approved, the following checks will be performed:

Check	Purpose
Schema Validation	Verify data structure
Missing Values	Identify incomplete data
Duplicate Detection	Remove repeated records
Label Verification	Ensure correct annotations
Distribution Analysis	Identify imbalance
Leakage Detection	Prevent data leakage
Split Verification	Prevent train/test contamination

8. Model Evaluation

Models will be evaluated using appropriate metrics such as:

Accuracy
Precision
Recall
F1-Score
Confusion Matrix
MAE / RMSE for prediction tasks

For the student-support system, we may also evaluate:

Response correctness
Response relevance
Robustness
Consistency
Response time

9. Regression Testing

Whenever the model, dataset, or preprocessing pipeline is updated, previously verified test cases will be executed again.

Old Model
   ↓
Baseline Results
   ↓
New Model
   ↓
Run Benchmark & Test Cases
   ↓
Compare Results
   ↓
Approve / Improve / Reject

This helps ensure that new changes do not reduce existing system performance.

